:: StoryTitle
Recipe Meter

:: StoryData
{
  "format": "Harlowe",
  "format-version": "3.3.9",
  "start": "Day",
  "zoom": 1
}

:: Setup [startup] {"position":"25,25","size":"100,100"}
<!-- STEP 1: the starting value. Use 0 to 100. -->
(set: $energy to 70)

:: Energy Meter [footer] {"position":"25,150","size":"100,100"}
<!-- STEP 3: this draws the bar at the bottom of EVERY passage (because of the footer tag). -->
Energy: $energy
(if: $energy < 30)[(print: '<div class="bar"><div class="fill low" style="width:' + (str: $energy) + '%"></div></div>')](else:)[(print: '<div class="bar"><div class="fill" style="width:' + (str: $energy) + '%"></div></div>')]

:: Day {"position":"150,25","size":"100,100"}
Your shift starts. What do you do?

<!-- STEP 4: change the number when the player picks something. (max: 0, ...) stops it going below 0. (min: 100, ...) stops it going above 100. -->
(link: "Work a double shift (-30)")[(set: $energy to (max: 0, $energy - 30))(goto: "Day")]
(link: "Take a break (+20)")[(set: $energy to (min: 100, $energy + 20))(goto: "Day")]

:: StoryStylesheet [stylesheet]
/* STEP 2: what the bar looks like */
.bar {
  width: 250px;            /* how long the bar is */
  height: 20px;            /* how thick the bar is */
  background: #444;        /* colour of the empty part */
  border: 2px solid white;
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.fill {
  height: 100%;
  background: #3cb371;     /* colour of the full part (green) */
}
.fill.low {
  background: #e53935;     /* colour when it's low (red) */
}
